docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T13.log:4215:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2720:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:669:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QHgJUDU2Z1BZn1GKKokHZ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012eScWFNCfoznDfAaZ3YQCU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T57.md","content":"# T57 — Phase 8 — Redesigned get_context_capsule + get_docs_capsule + find_relevant_tests + impact_from_diff\n\n**Phase:** 8\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** R55\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task redesigns the four discovery workflow tools (`get_context_capsule`, `get_docs_capsule`, `find_relevant_tests`, `impact_from_diff`) on top of the Phase 1–7 substrates so that each tool returns a compact bundle by default with deliberate expansion handles, rather than dumping broad slices of files. Spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties requires \"every workflow bundle is compact by default with deliberate expansion handles\" and spec §Phase 8 DoD requires workflows that \"produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping.\" Without this redesign, discovery calls remain the dominant tool-call cost in Phase 9 metrics and the success criterion \"40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads\" cannot be met.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Every workflow bundle is compact by default with deliberate expansion handles.\" (spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties)\n\n> \"Phase 8 Deliverables: redesigned versions of context, change planning, scenario tracing, failure diagnosis, docs retrieval, test selection, impact analysis, and playbook generation; workflow composition over graph, event, memory, and working-memory substrates.\"\n\n> \"Every tool response should support: compact rendering, full structured JSON, context handles, stable expansion targets, budget controls, diagnostic explanations where useful.\" (spec §MCP Surface)\n\n> \"Definition of done: common coding tasks require fewer manual discovery calls; workflows produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R55 (Phase 7 verification engine review) — verification statuses must be surfaced inside every discovery bundle so stale memory cannot appear as trusted guidance.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/context_capsule.rs` — current heuristic context capsule, retained as a compatibility shim per the T02 compatibility policy.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/docs_capsule.rs` — current docs capsule.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/find_relevant_tests.rs` — current relevant-test discovery.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/impact_from_diff.rs` — current diff-based impact analysis.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — MCP tool registration.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs` — context-handle cache, reused for stable expansion targets.\n  - Phase 1 identity types; Phase 2 event writer; Phase 4 retrieval pipeline (intent classifier, anchor resolver, hybrid candidate retrieval, compact response shaper); Phase 7 verification engine.\n  - T56 shared `WorkflowBundle`, `Pivot`, `MemoryHighlight`, `EventEpisode`, `RiskNote`, `ExpansionHint` types.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Single source of truth, §No broken windows, §Schema parity, §Observability; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references; `AGENTS.md` backward-compatibility discipline.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 8 and §MCP Tool Contract Principles in full. Reuse the shared bundle types from T56 (`WorkflowBundle`, `Pivot`, `MemoryHighlight`, `EventEpisode`, `RiskNote`, `ExpansionHint`) so all eight Phase 8 tools share one schema surface; do not duplicate the structs in `workflow_v2/`.\n2. Implement `get_context_capsule` in `workflow_v2/context_capsule.rs`: take a free-form task or file/symbol anchor list, run the Phase 4 intent classifier + anchor resolver, retrieve compact candidates from graph + memory + docs + events, score them, and produce a compact bundle with at most N pivots (default 8, configurable via budget control). Each pivot must carry an inclusion reason and a stable expansion handle. Support `mode: \"focused\" | \"compact\" | \"full\" | \"diagnostic\"` per spec §MCP Surface render modes.\n3. Implement `get_docs_capsule` in `workflow_v2/docs_capsule.rs`: anchor on doc sections rather than code symbols, traverse `documents` and `mentions` edges to surface adjacent prose and ADRs, and include code anchors that the cited sections reference. Output bundle must distinguish \"doc primary\" pivots from \"code-referenced\" pivots so the consumer knows where the authoritative text lives.\n4. Implement `find_relevant_tests` in `workflow_v2/relevant_tests.rs`: accept either a file/symbol set or a diff, traverse `tested_by` edges in the Phase 1 graph, combine with `co_changed_with` evidence from the event log, score by graph proximity + past test-failure frequency, and return ranked test files with the verification command needed to run each (e.g. `cargo test -p X --lib mod::tests::test_name`). Spec §Measurable Success Criteria targets 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks — the API must record per-recommendation provenance so T69 regression tests can measure recall.\n5. Implement `impact_from_diff` in `workflow_v2/impact_from_diff.rs`: accept a diff or list of changed files/symbols, walk dependent edges (`calls`, `imports`, `implements`, `extends`, `type_ref`, `depends_on`) up to a bounded depth (spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties forbids unbounded traversal on hot paths), attach affected tests via `tested_by`, attach affected docs via `documents`, and surface high-impact warnings as `RiskNote`s.\n6. Each tool must emit `AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ContextBundleReturned`, and `MemoryRetrieved` events via the Phase 2 `EventWriter`. Hot-path budget per spec §Phase 2 DoD: ≤5ms P99 event-write overhead on `get_context_capsule`.\n7. Each tool must register a stable context handle in `rpc/context_cache.rs` so `expand_context` can fetch the next delta cheaply per spec §MCP Surface \"stable expansion targets\" and spec §First Implementation Slice \"Compact memory inclusion reasons in existing workflow tools.\"\n8. Register the four `workflow_v2` tools in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`; keep legacy implementations registered with deprecation flags per the T02 compatibility policy.\n9. In `workflow_v2/discovery_workflows_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) round-trip each tool's request/response through serde; (b) assert default render mode is compact and bundle size stays under the configured budget; (c) assert `get_context_capsule` returns expansion handles that `expand_context` can dereference; (d) assert `find_relevant_tests` recovers known golden tests for fixture repos; (e) assert `impact_from_diff` bounded-traversal cap is enforced; (f) assert no stale/contradicted memory appears without a stale label.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/context_capsule.rs` — redesigned `get_context_capsule` with intent-aware compact bundles and render-mode support.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/docs_capsule.rs` — redesigned `get_docs_capsule` distinguishing doc-primary and code-referenced pivots.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/relevant_tests.rs` — redesigned `find_relevant_tests` returning ranked tests with verification commands and per-recommendation provenance for T69 metric tests.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/impact_from_diff.rs` — redesigned `impact_from_diff` with bounded traversal, affected-test attachment, and high-impact `RiskNote`s.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/discovery_workflows_tests.rs` — unit + golden tests covering schema, compact-by-default, handle round-trip, fixture recovery, bounded traversal, and stale-label discipline.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/context_capsule.rs` — confirms the redesigned `get_context_capsule` exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/impact_from_diff.rs` — confirms the redesigned `impact_from_diff` exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::workflow_v2::discovery_workflows_tests` — every discovery-workflow test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split per-tool when needed).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: reuse the shared `WorkflowBundle` schema from T56; do not introduce a parallel response type unless explicitly justified.\n- No silent error handling — every retrieval/traversal/event-writer failure returns a typed error and surfaces as a `RiskNote` rather than being swallowed.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`ContextCapsuleRequest::render_mode`, not `ContextCapsuleRequest::mode_str`).\n- For SQLite: not applicable directly; storage access goes through Phase 2/3/7 APIs.\n- Observability: each tool emits `tracing::info!` spans with `tool`, `task_id`, `session_id`, `bundle_size_bytes`, `pivot_count`, `handle_count` fields.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2`, `## MCP Surface`, and `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties` in module doc comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: compact-by-default + expansion handles + render modes are all implemented in this task; no \"later optimization\" is permitted to ship them later.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; legacy `get_context_capsule` / `get_docs_capsule` / `find_relevant_tests` / `impact_from_diff` continue to respond per the T02 compatibility policy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4964,"cache_read_input_tokens":59231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4964,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"1fcd67dc-db59-4f9e-ba4f-c866f1a722c9","request_id":"req_011Cb7MrQcmeoxoHC3sgQkGJ","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
