docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5848:This task creates the canonical metrics module that collects every assistant-usefulness signal required by spec §Phase 9. Without a single module owning these signals, downstream tasks (T66 benchmark fixtures, T67 MCP surface, T68 CLI report, T69 regression tests) would each invent their own definitions and diverge. The module turns the event log + memory access history + workflow outcomes into the nine required signals named in spec §Phase 9: tool calls per successful task, irrelevant files opened per task, relevant anchor recall, memory inclusion precision, memory later-used rate, stale memory surfaced rate, contradiction missed rate, tests recommended versus tests needed, and workflow success after first plan.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5873:2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/mod.rs` exporting `signals`, the `MetricSignal` enum, the `MetricValue` struct, and the `MetricsCollector` aggregator. Doc-comment the module with a reference to spec §Phase 9.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5874:3. In `metrics/signals.rs`, define `pub enum MetricSignal` with one variant per spec-required signal: `ToolCallsPerSuccessfulTask`, `IrrelevantFilesOpenedPerTask`, `RelevantAnchorRecall`, `MemoryInclusionPrecision`, `MemoryLaterUsedRate`, `StaleMemorySurfacedRate`, `ContradictionMissedRate`, `TestsRecommendedVsNeeded`, `WorkflowSuccessAfterFirstPlan`. Derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Clone`, `Copy`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Hash`. Implement `MetricSignal::as_str()` returning the canonical snake_case wire name used by the T67 MCP surface and the T68 CLI report.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5875:4. Define `pub struct MetricValue { signal: MetricSignal, value: Option<f64>, denominator: Option<u64>, sample_count: u64, source: MetricSource, computed_at: DateTime<Utc>, reason_if_null: Option<String> }`. The `Option<f64>` value supports honest reporting when no data is available — never fabricate zeros. The `source` field discriminates `EventLog`, `MemoryStore`, `WorkflowOutcome`, `Verifier`, `SessionMetrics`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5886:6. Implement `pub struct MetricsCollector { … }` exposing `collect(scope: MetricScope, signals: &[MetricSignal]) -> Vec<MetricValue>`. `MetricScope` mirrors the §Memory Graph scope taxonomy (`session | branch | repo | user | organization`) plus an optional time range.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5887:7. Honor the spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bounds: no unbounded event-log scan on hot paths. Every collector applies a scope filter and a configurable maximum sample size, with explicit `incomplete: true` on the `MetricValue` when truncated.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5888:8. In `metrics/signals_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) every `MetricSignal` variant has a deterministic collector; (b) collectors return `None` with a reason when no data is available rather than fabricating zero; (c) each collector returns the spec-defined value on a hand-crafted event fixture; (d) scope filters prevent cross-scope leakage; (e) sample-size bounds are honored.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5892:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/mod.rs` — module root exporting `signals`, `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricSource`, `MetricsCollector`, `MetricScope`; doc-comment cites spec §Phase 9.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5893:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/signals.rs` — `MetricSignal` enum with all nine spec-required variants, `MetricValue` struct, deterministic collector implementations, scope and sample-size bounds.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5906:- Schema parity: `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricSource`, `MetricScope` derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Debug`, `Clone`; every public field has a doc comment; wire names match the strings used by T67/T68.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T60.log:5909:- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`MetricSignal::RelevantAnchorRecall`, not `MetricSignal::AnchorRec`).
